ad","pageTitle":"Greek Yogurt Bread","path":"\/greek-yogurt-bread","text":"Could I use whole wheat flour as part or all of the flour?","thread":{"-NY4wfcA8e5fTIF96ytZ":{"author":"Melisa","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/greek-yogurt-bread","path":"\/greek-yogurt-bread","text":"Hi Stan! I'm sure that you could use some wheat flour as a part of this recipe. It will change the fluffy white bread texture the more whole wheat flour is used so expect the color to become darker and the texture to become more dense. You might try substituting only 1\/2 cup to start and work up from there if you like how it turns out. I'd love to know how it works out for you!","time":1686948199025,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userPic":"$profile:7ab789456869965485e7389825cfb8d0.jpg","userType":"email"}},"time":1686941307601,"userId":"59b81f17774cf8544098c9c0d76627b9","userType":"email"},"-NdHP5UWkpz1zM4kuJ66":{"author":"Marie","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/greek-yogurt-bread","pageTitle":"Greek Yogurt Bread","path":"\/greek-yogurt-bread","rating":5,"text":"forgot to the part for yogurt only to find it had spoiled! Substituted 1\/2cup mayonnaise? OGG best bread ever!!!!❤❤❤","time":1693599689368,"userId":"f21b6c7e78c8a5dce90ea1ce1af76453","userType":"email","voteData":{"6ac99fe51d8a62def71c16c80a91292b948ede89a089b71634fcbe908b794f59":1},"votes":1},"-O8m0TlkbVJKgKgZSRZP":{"author":"Elaine","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/greek-yogurt-bread","pageTitle":"Greek Yogurt Bread","path":"\/greek-yogurt-bread","text":"When you remove the dough from the mixer is the dough suppose to be a little sticky. It’s my first time making this recipe and want to make sure I’m doing it right\n","thread":{"-O8m91ItwGu5RtdvEztX":{"author":"Melisa Smith ","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/greek-yogurt-bread","pageTitle":"Greek Yogurt Bread","path":"\/greek-yogurt-bread","text":"Yes, it is somewhat sticky. After kneading in a little flour before rising it the first time, it will become more tacky. ","time":1728492086628,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userType":"email"}},"time":1728489844217,"userId":"visitor","userType":"anonymous","voteData":{"a5f70544b8219c42fae8956425cbcd5997f8a11f7e912965101b13c561fffc12":1,"ba69514b26b73fc12322425f2022add370de05388bc63947b8ef2df1f6d7e96d":1},"votes":2},"-OAmCRSy6zTW2_62KCAq":{"author":"Grace","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/greek-yogurt-bread#google_vignette","pageTitle":"Greek Yogurt Bread","path":"\/greek-yogurt-bread","rating":5,"text":"I’ve made this a couple of times over the last 2 weeks. It’s the best bread I’ve ever made. \n\nThat being said, I do have a question. The dough just doesn’t seem right when using the amount of flour you call for. I’ve added an extra 1.5 cups of AP to each batch. After reading the other comments, I’m now questioning myself rather than your ingredients list.  Is the dough really supposed to be that loose and sticky?  There’s no pulling away from the bowl at all. \n","thread":{"-OAreBb2qAvAFRFAmoR_":{"author":"Melisa Smith","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/greek-yogurt-bread","pageTitle":"Greek Yogurt Bread","path":"\/greek-yogurt-bread","text":"Hi Grace! I'm glad you love my recipe for Greek Yogurt Bread and yes, it's a little loose and sticky when I move it to the 1\/4 cup of flour to knead. The difference in how dry your flour is can make a big difference though and you may be needing to adjust your flour for that reason. Also, my experience with using actual bread flour is that it also makes my dough more sticky. You could try replacing some or all of the bread flour with AP and you might be happier with how the dough handles. ","time":1730731585124,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userType":"email"},"-OAsWZfOe__bqgHFgHSt":{"author":"Grace","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/greek-yogurt-bread#google_vignette","pageTitle":"Greek Yogurt Bread",